From: Alexander Schiffhauer <Alexander.Schiffhauer@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] workspace: retry a rejected output configuration without wide
 color gamut

A driver can accept a mode on its own and reject it together with the
BT.2020 colorspace. NVIDIA 615.78 does this for a Pro Display XDR at
6016x3384 behind a DisplayPort-to-USB4 input: the atomic test passes in
SDR and with HDR metadata alone, and fails with EINVAL once the Colorspace
property is BT2020_RGB. The stored configuration has wide color gamut on,
so the output is refused, the low-bandwidth retry cannot allocate buffers
on NVIDIA either, and the display stays dark.

When applying a configuration fails, turn wide color gamut off on the
outputs that request it and try once more before giving up.
---
--- a/src/workspace.cpp
+++ b/src/workspace.cpp
@@ -688,6 +688,24 @@
         }
 
         result = applyOutputConfiguration(cfg);
+        if (!result && result.error().code != OutputErrorCode::NotActive) {
+            // Some drivers accept a mode but reject it together with the BT.2020
+            // colorspace. A lit output with a narrower gamut beats a dark one.
+            bool reduced = false;
+            for (const auto &output : std::as_const(toEnable)) {
+                const auto changes = cfg.changeSet(output);
+                if (changes->wideColorGamut.value_or(output->wideColorGamut())) {
+                    changes->wideColorGamut = false;
+                    reduced = true;
+                }
+            }
+            if (reduced) {
+                if (const auto retried = applyOutputConfiguration(cfg)) {
+                    qCWarning(KWIN_CORE, "Applied the output configuration without wide color gamut after the driver rejected it");
+                    result = retried;
+                }
+            }
+        }
         if (result) {
             if (type == OutputConfigurationStore::ConfigType::Generated) {
                 const bool hasInternal = std::any_of(outputs.begin(), outputs.end(), [](BackendOutput *o) {
